  "event_layout": "Opcode followed by its exact argument arity, then 74 state words before the scripted mutation. Execute: index, animate, raw low-byte carry, opaque DWORD, finite double low/high. Bridge: index. Road: index, opaque DWORD, finite double low/high. Integer: signed integer bits. Put: instance, three PA-name bytes packed little-endian, third argument, initialized type and node words, finite double low/high.",
  "state_layout": "Arena and selected index, then two arenas each with six records at indices -1,0,1,499,500,501. Each record contributes signed16 row, column and first-unit type; DWORD count and instance tail. Twelve FNV-1a32 fingerprints cover complete 404-byte paths. Final output adds the function result and two complete-arena fingerprints.",
  "exact_no_write_check": "Both original and native adapters capture all bytes of two 0x90000-byte arenas and gameData/selection after initialization and each boundary mutation. They compare those bytes/globals exactly before every boundary and at return. Fingerprints in the compact trace are separate observations, not claims of literal full-byte trace serialization. The local PA array is not included in world-state guards.",
  "value_payload": "The original reserves 24 local bytes and initializes only type 1 at+4 and integer-node DWORD at+8. The scalar PutSlot consumer, constraint and error-print paths consume only those initialized words. The boundary reads only value[1]/value[2]; it never copies or inspects untouched words. The historical pa_value[8]=a2 models saved incoming ECX outside the local 24-byte buffer.",
  "opaque_argument_recovery": "Incoming EBP survives the target and is present at Execute and Road. Original Execute carries a3; the historical native caller passed index in that fourth argument. In all 12 eligible distinct-argument cases, the unchanged-before trace differs only at Execute argument 4, with every other recorded word equal. This is a defined caller-boundary mismatch, not an uninitialized local. The actual gameplay effect of this opaque argument is not established by the isolated adapter.",
  "before_comparison": "Every profile contains 115 unchanged-before exact original matches and 12 defined fourth-argument-only mismatches. Thirteen high-address cases are excluded from before equivalence:10 trigger signed integer addition overflow and 3 sign-extend a negative computed record into an invalid 64-bit pointer. Exact earliest-read classifications are listed separately. Isolated diagnostic probes retain UBSan or pointer-fault evidence; no patched-before body is an oracle.",
  "address_scope": "Two fixed arenas at0x10000000 and0x7FFE0000, each0x90000 bytes, back records -1,0,1,499,500,501 and their complete payloads. Original address operations wrap to 32 bits. The caller reads entry count/coordinates and executes before checking index 0..500 inclusive. Nonzero raw counts are tested only for truth here because path-consuming callees are boundaries. No claim is made that arbitrary unbacked pointers or every uint32 index is safe.",
  "return_scope": "Empty returns 0 without calls. All nonempty normal-return cases return 1 after the applicable boundaries, regardless of Road or slot-put results. Actual Bridge returns 0/1; other script values are conditional truthiness probes. Actual Road returns 0/1; other script values are conditional ignored-result probes. Integer results are opaque node words; the five named raw-bit cases do not establish valid actual CLIPS nodes.",
  "read_order": "Entry count and signed16 coordinate reads share one stable phase. After Execute, the first-unit type uses fresh gameData; after Bridge and optional Road the coordinate comparison uses fresh gameData; after Integer the instance tail uses fresh gameData. ESI/EDI preserve entry coordinates, and ECX=1/EDX=offset survive Integer. Later callee mutations must not be overwritten, revalidated or used to change the unconditional nonempty return.",
  "compile_policy": "GCC13 and Clang18 at O0/O2, Wall/Wextra/Werror, UBSan with only the established packed-layout alignment exception. The native fixture maps free fixed addresses with MAP_FIXED_NOREPLACE. No unused/uninitialized diagnostic suppression or scalar-buffer initialization workaround is used.",
  "evidence": "artifacts/readability/road-functions-20260906/batch-16/original-proof/, test-audit/fresh-coordinate-extension/, negative-controls/fresh-coordinate-extension/ and before-domain-probes/. Private initial 133/138 measurements and the surviving cached-post-query-base sensitivity failure are retained. Two appended coordinate-change cases close that measured coverage gap. Public tests need only tracked sources and this JSON; no original bytes or retail assets are required.",
  "limits": [
    "Only the unchanged original 288-byte caller and native caller body execute. Execute, Bridge, Road, Integer and Put are recording/mutation boundaries. Actual movement, pathfinding, map costs, Road construction, CLIPS interning/storage and rendering do not execute.",
    "Finite double bits include signed zero, subnormals and finite extremes. The original adapter preserves incoming x87 state at boundaries. NaNs, infinities and changes to the floating-point environment are outside this proof.",
    "Callback mutations test fresh caller reads and preservation; they do not claim that every scripted mutation occurs in unmodified gameplay. There is no asynchronous or volatile read contract.",
    "The record 721..724 tail is observed as a slot API instance argument. A broader ownership or structure interpretation remains unproven.",
    "These caller traces prove no arrival, runtime route, visual fidelity or campaign milestone."
